# ogustOS Licensing & Distribution Notice

`ogustOS` is an aggregate Linux distribution composed of original build/system
engineering code, the Linux kernel, and upstream open-source and redistributable
software packages.

---

## 1. Original `ogustOS` Code, Installer, Scripts & Branding (`GPL-3.0-or-later`)

Copyright (C) 2026 Ogun Aydin

All original scripts, installer code (`bin/ogust`, `bin/ogust-install`,
`scripts/*.sh`), system configuration files (`etc/`, `apt/`), and visual
branding assets (`branding/`) in this repository are free software: you can
redistribute them and/or modify them under the terms of the **GNU General Public
License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the
License, or (at your option) any later version (`GPL-3.0-or-later`)**.

---

## 2. Linux Kernel Configuration & Patches (`GPL-2.0-only`)

All Linux kernel configurations (`kernel/config-*-ogustOS`,
`kernel/fragments/*.config`) and kernel source patches (`kernel/patches/`) are
licensed strictly under the **GNU General Public License version 2.0 only
(`GPL-2.0-only`)**, matching the upstream Linux kernel (`kernel.org`), the BORE
scheduler (`firelzrd/bore-scheduler`), and TCP BBRv3 (`google/bbr`).

---

## 3. Mere Aggregation of Upstream Packages & Firmware

Under **Section 5 of the GNU General Public License (v2 and v3, "Mere
Aggregation")**, inclusion of upstream packages from Debian, Pardus, and
third-party repositories (including `linux-firmware`, `amd64-microcode`,
`intel-microcode`, `steam-installer`, and `google-chrome-stable`) in an
`ogustOS` installation image (`.iso` / `filesystem.squashfs`) constitutes an
aggregate distribution. Each individual software package retains its respective
upstream license as documented in `/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright` on the
installed system.
